<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Simón de Anda y Salazar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1709">1709</a>–<a href="/years/1776">1776</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Simón de Anda y Salazar was a Spanish judge and colonial governor in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philippines">Philippines</a>. When the British took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manila">Manila</a> in 1762 he escaped to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pampanga">Pampanga</a>, declared himself governor and organised resistance from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bacolor">Bacolor</a> until the British left in 1764. He later served as governor-general of the Philippines from 1770 until his death.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/simon-de-anda-y-salazar.jpg" alt="Simón de Anda y Salazar" width="320" height="416" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author (currently held at the collection of Bernardo Estornés Lasa) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sim%C3%B3n_de_Anda_y_Salazar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
